Dataset
For dengue outbreak prediction, data is collected from three sites.
1)	Integrated Disease Surveillance Programme Data (IDSP): IDSP provides weekly dengue case counts and sanitation reports by state from 2019 to 2025, essential for tracking disease spread.
2)	Meteorological Data from Open-Meteo.com: Weekly weather data, including rainfall, humidity, and temperature, are used to analyze correlations with dengue incidence.
3)	Sanitation Reports from Swachh Bharat Mission: Sanitation and cleanliness data from Swachh Bharat Mission-Gramin helps to understand how environmental factors influence dengue transmission.


